WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.560
The hype behind "Elden Ring" continues&nbsp;
to build as the release date draws near.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.160
What spoilers have already made their way&nbsp;
online? Keep watching if you're hungry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.440
for every morsel of information&nbsp;
about this long-awaited game.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:17.040
During the game's closed network test, players&nbsp;
with jailbroken PS4s datamined "Elden Ring"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:22.080
and uncovered some closely-guarded secrets. From&nbsp;
Software clearly understood the risk of players&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.720
digging too deeply into the test run, which&nbsp;
is why the developers placed a giant bear in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.760
the game that would kill any players who managed&nbsp;
to find a way outside of the test's boundaries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.320
Not too surprising considering the&nbsp;
developers' enduring sadistic tendencies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.320
But really though, after all the things "Dark&nbsp;
Souls" players have been through over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.120
is a ferocious bear all that intimidating?

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.000
"Hey Ron! I'm riding a furry tractor!"

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.680
Unfortunately for From Software, the developers&nbsp;
couldn't predict this new PS4 exploit. The Verge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:57.680
released a report about the PS4 jailbreak on&nbsp;
December 14, 2021, and spoilers for "Elden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.800
Ring" began making rounds just a few days later.&nbsp;
Of course, until the game actually releases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.040
From Software could certainly make as many&nbsp;
changes as it wants to the leaked material.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.680
The "Elden Ring" story trailer introduces&nbsp;
the basics of the game's backstory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:16.480
It opens by revealing that the fall of the world's&nbsp;
demigods began with Godwyn the Golden's death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:21.600
Newly leaked information from the game, however,&nbsp;
seems to reveal that Godwyn is very much alive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.240
The leaks show that Godwyn will actually be the&nbsp;
game's primary blacksmith, and players will rely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.640
on his abilities to upgrade their weapons&nbsp;
— similar to the process in "Dark Souls."

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:34.320
Considering that the game's trailer claimed&nbsp;
that Godwyn had died after the rune of death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.640
was stolen, how does he factor into the&nbsp;
rest of the game's story? Another audio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.600
file features Godwyn quietly rambling about&nbsp;
a Grail and his ability to smith weapons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.200
The speech is in line with characters&nbsp;
from previous "Souls" games who lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.160
their minds after taking&nbsp;
part in horrifying events.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:56.400
"For a very long time, I was trapped within&nbsp;
the Crystal Golem. From my home I was taken,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.120
and banished to a plane of distortion."

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.680
Perhaps tragedy left Godwyn's mind damaged,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:06.240
even as his body lives on to assist future&nbsp;
travelers. And maybe that's why the trailer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:10.960
shows Godwyn's corpse opening its eyes as&nbsp;
black liquid oozes from beneath its eyelids.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.000
One of the biggest changes that "Elden Ring"&nbsp;
will introduce to the "Souls" sub-genre is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.880
an open world that puts a heavy emphasis on&nbsp;
exploration. Since the first "Dark Souls" game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:25.040
From Software has been crafting worlds&nbsp;
that seamlessly interlink different areas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:30.400
but "Elden Ring" will offer an open world in&nbsp;
the more traditional sense. In November 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:35.360
Bandai Namco finally released a gameplay preview&nbsp;
of "Elden Ring" that gave players a taste of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:40.080
the variety of locations they would encounter&nbsp;
throughout the game. The recent data-mining leaks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:45.680
have revealed even more details about what's&nbsp;
in store for adventurers come February 2022.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:50.080
"We happy?"
"Yeah, we happy."

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:54.640
One file that's been leaked makes reference to&nbsp;
"the other Eternal City." The speakers say that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:59.680
the city hides a "cradle chalice," and though the&nbsp;
importance of the chalice has yet to be revealed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.000
From Software fans will likely remember the&nbsp;
importance of chalices in "Bloodborne." In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.200
that game, chalices were used to generate dungeons&nbsp;
that could be explored for unique loot and bosses.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:13.760
Some other "Elden Ring" dialogue has been leaked&nbsp;
in a text file, and an unknown speaker makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:18.240
reference to a secret path that leads through a&nbsp;
well to the meeting place of "the Great Caravan"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:22.240
somewhere "under the capital." Secret&nbsp;
paths and underground cities are nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:27.120
new to veterans of From Software's previous&nbsp;
games, but we'll have to wait until February,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:31.840
or the next round of leaks, to piece together&nbsp;
how the Great Caravan fits into the game's story.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.760
From Software's games tend to have&nbsp;
stories that are rich with details&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.920
but difficult to understand. They're often&nbsp;
told through item descriptions and opaque&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:43.920
bits of dialogue threaded throughout the&nbsp;
game, which turns piecing things together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:48.160
into a challenging mini game of its own.&nbsp;
That makes this particular leak especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:52.800
exciting for anyone who wants a deeper&nbsp;
understanding of "Elden Ring's" main story.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.360
"I offer you an accord."

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:01.120
Datamined files from the game's closed network&nbsp;
test contain an entire quest's worth of dialogue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:06.160
The dialogue comes from Millicent, a young&nbsp;
girl suffering from "scarlet rot," and Gowry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:11.680
the sage who raised her. Millicent is the daughter&nbsp;
of Malenia who rules part of the Lands Between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:16.960
with her five sisters. Malenia once fought the&nbsp;
giant Lord Radahn, and one day she will replace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:22.080
her mother Marika as Queen. Gowry asks that&nbsp;
the players kill Millicent when Malenia ascends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:27.520
to the throne. Only then will Millicent, quote,&nbsp;
"begin to flower" and become a "scarlet valkyrie."

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.800
The branching dialogue seems to reveal&nbsp;
that players have the option to either&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:35.040
do as Gowry asks or to help Millicent&nbsp;
escape her fate. There's no indication&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:39.680
of how central this particular questline is to&nbsp;
the main story, but fans already know from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:44.640
game's official description that Queen Marika&nbsp;
the Eternal and her daughters are a main focus.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:49.280
If the leaks are to be believed, many fan&nbsp;
favorite methods of mowing down enemies from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:53.760
the "Souls" games will be returning to "Elden&nbsp;
Ring." Data mining has revealed many of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:57.600
various weapon classes that the Tarnished&nbsp;
will have at their disposal as they wander&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:02.400
about the Lands Between slaying monsters. Many&nbsp;
classes, from the greatsword to the warhammer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:07.440
are "Souls" series regulars. Others, like the bow&nbsp;
and crossbow, have seen their mechanical ups and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:12.800
downs over the years. There are also some exciting&nbsp;
new additions, including the glintstone staff.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:15.040
"Ugh, that is so gnarly."

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:19.680
Another returning combat enhancement is the&nbsp;
ability to infuse weapons with various magical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:24.800
properties or elements. Players can make their&nbsp;
blades ignite into flames, poison enemies, or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:29.760
deal extreme physical damage. For anyone building&nbsp;
a character with a darker aim on dealing death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:34.480
blood and occult infusions will likely work&nbsp;
perfectly, though gamers don't yet have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:39.360
clear understanding of how they augment damage.&nbsp;
There were no major surprises in the weapons and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:44.320
infusions leak, but there are more than enough new&nbsp;
touches to get fans' imaginations running wild.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:51.840
The bosses of "Elden Ring" will likely provide&nbsp;
some of the game's most memorable moments.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:58.480
"Someone must extinguish thy&nbsp;
flame. Let it be Margit The Fell."

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:02.560
There'll be no shortage of monstrous&nbsp;
death dealers for players to tackle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:07.680
during their exploration of the lands between, but&nbsp;
another spoiler claims to reveal the identities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.760
of the six main bosses who will need to&nbsp;
be dispatched to obtain the Great Runes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:15.680
Players will take on the Golden&nbsp;
Lord Godric, the Moon Lord Rennala,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:22.000
the Blood Lord Mohg, the Grace Lord Morgott, the&nbsp;
Chaos Lord Hoarah Loux, and the Giant Lord Radahn.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.920
The last of these intimidating warriors&nbsp;
can be seen in the game's story trailer.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:29.040
The "Elden Ring" leaks uncovered a&nbsp;
few other small insights into two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:33.200
of the bosses. There are three NPCs&nbsp;
listed as Lord Rennala's children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:37.360
meaning that Rennala's boss battle could be&nbsp;
one to look out for. It wouldn't be the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:42.000
time From Software put players toe-to-toe&nbsp;
with multiple bosses in a single fight.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:46.560
Radahn's strength level is supported by&nbsp;
another audio file where a female NPC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:50.320
describes his battle, and victory,&nbsp;
with a constellation of stars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:54.880
Either she's speaking metaphorically, or Radahn&nbsp;
is even bigger than he appeared in the trailer.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:59.040
A massive text file containing&nbsp;
huge chunks of the game's dialogue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:03.680
was uncovered during the data-mining process.&nbsp;
There are pages of text to pore over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:07.920
but none of them label which characters are&nbsp;
speaking which lines. Even without that key&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:12.080
information, however, keen readers have been&nbsp;
able to pull out some inferred story beats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:16.160
from the file's disjointed lines, and&nbsp;
luckily for anyone truly committed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.880
uncovering as much information as possible,&nbsp;
another leak can work as a helpful guide.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:24.880
A list of every NPC in the game has been&nbsp;
revealed, and it can tell players quite a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:29.040
lot about what to expect throughout their&nbsp;
time in the Lands Between. Queen Marika,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:33.200
the various lords, and Millicent all stand&nbsp;
out because their names come up more often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.960
than others in the dialogue that's been&nbsp;
revealed so far. Characters with names&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:41.680
like Narrator and Talking Corpses are little&nbsp;
more than interesting mysteries at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:47.200
but others might be familiar to "Souls" fans —&nbsp;
get ready to say hello to Patches once again.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:51.440
"Oh! The demons haven't got&nbsp;
you, have they? I'm in luck."

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:56.160
The extensive NPC list is also a reminder&nbsp;
of the game's scale. There are over five&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:00.800
dozen NPCs named, and it's hard to say&nbsp;
for sure that everyone has been included.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:06.400
Sometimes a soundtrack can tell a story of its&nbsp;
own. Music can make or break a game's tone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:11.200
and the music of "Elden Ring" has high standards&nbsp;
to live up to. Half a dozen soundtrack files have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:15.120
been leaked, and they give an instant sense&nbsp;
of how the game will feel. In one track,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:19.360
epic choral swells create a grandiose&nbsp;
but unrelentingly eerie atmosphere.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:22.720
Another track that sounds like it came&nbsp;
straight out of a bloody fight scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:27.360
uses a combination of chorus vocals and&nbsp;
rhythmic strings to build the tension.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:32.080
Composer Yuka Kitamura's talents are on full&nbsp;
display in all of the music that has been leaked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:37.440
so far. It's no surprise that Kitamura also worked&nbsp;
on the soundtrack for "Bloodborne," and clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:42.080
the horror elements that inspired the previous&nbsp;
game's sound have been brought into "Elden Ring."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:47.280
Until Bandai Namco releases more in-game footage&nbsp;
or a playable demo that's open to the public,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:52.400
listening to these tracks is the closest fans&nbsp;
can get to experiencing the game firsthand.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:56.640
You don't really need leaks to tell you how&nbsp;
"Elden Ring" ends. After exploring every inch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.640 --> 00:09:00.480
of the Lands Between and slaying countless&nbsp;
monsters and foes, it will all come down to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:06.160
one last epic boss battle. "Dark Souls" had Gwyn,&nbsp;
Lord of Cinder, while "Bloodborne" had Gehrman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:10.480
Every "Souls" game has its own memorable&nbsp;
final boss, and there's no reason to expect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:15.280
that "Elden Ring" would suddenly abandon this&nbsp;
integral piece of the tried-and-true formula.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:16.560
"Well, I'm convinced."

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:19.680
For all the information pulled from&nbsp;
the game's closed network test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:24.240
dataminers apparently came up empty on&nbsp;
the question of the game's true big bad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:27.920
Instead of giving a definitive answer, fans&nbsp;
have surmised that there are several different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:33.120
possibilities, ranging from Queen Marika&nbsp;
the Eternal to Malenia's many daughters.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:36.240
Queen Marika might be the&nbsp;
obvious choice for a final boss,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:41.280
since her offspring rule the various regions of&nbsp;
the Lands Between, but FromSoftware isn't exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:46.000
known for making obvious decisions with their&nbsp;
stories. For now, the final battle in "Elden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:50.480
Ring" remains a mystery — but the leaks have&nbsp;
definitely given fans a few credible hints.

